            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Report on seven patients with giantcell arteritis. An ophthalmodynamographic finding typical for these aspects of case was recorded in all cases. In one-sided and permanently one-sided functional disturbances, too, a pathologically reduced pulsation volume on both sides could always be derived.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
